WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.860
Many Hindus believe that, long ago, sages
in deep meditation heard truths that

2
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.280
no human had composed.

3
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.910
Those truths became the Vedas.

4
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.080
Priests still recite them in
Sanskrit, with exact sound and accent.

5
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:20.560
Other texts tell of a prince in
exile and a great family war.

6
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.940
Hindus call these remembered.

7
00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.600
Some scriptures were heard,
and others remembered.

8
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.780
Why does the difference matter?

9
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.910
In this mission, you'll sort the great
Hindu texts into heard and remembered.

10
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.590
Then you'll weigh up which kind of
scripture matters more to Hindus today.

11
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.230
Your mission: find out why the difference
between heard and remembered scriptures

12
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.040
matters.
